; SW-155 / SW-156 / SW-157: bignum and bignum-rational literals, and
; number->string on a bignum-backed exact rational, must read/print
; identically between native and the VM. Before the fix the VM's own reader
; (lib/backend/vm_parser.c) read an int64-overflowing integer literal as an
; inexact double (SW-155), clamped a `/`-literal's overflowing numerator or
; denominator to atoll()'s overflow result (SW-156), and its number->string
; native path routed a VAL_RATIONAL/VAL_BIGNUM through a double-only
; as_number() that silently answers 0.0 for both tags (SW-157) — all three
; already correct on native.
(display 123456789012345678901234567890) (newline)
(display (exact? 123456789012345678901234567890)) (newline)
(display -123456789012345678901234567890) (newline)
(display (+ 123456789012345678901234567890 1)) (newline)
(display 1/123456789012345678901234567890) (newline)
(display (exact? 1/123456789012345678901234567890)) (newline)
(display 123456789012345678901234567891/7) (newline)
(display 246913578024691357802469135780/2) (newline)
(display (number->string (/ (expt 7 30) (expt 11 25)))) (newline)
(display (exact? (/ (expt 7 30) (expt 11 25)))) (newline)
(display (number->string (expt 2 100))) (newline)
